0003: ggml-cuda block_reduce paylasimli bellek yarisi (aynı girdi, farkli bayt)
Upstream: audio.cpp PR #837 (v0.9.2) / ggml #26385 duzeltmesinin v0.7.2'ye tasinmasi.
- softmax.cu soft_max_f32: iki block_reduce (MAX, SUM) ayni buf_iw'yi kullaniyor; arada __syncthreads.
- softmax.cu tek satir (parallelize_cols): MAX ve SUM icin ayri paylasimli bellek.
- norm.cu group_norm_f32: ikinci azaltma ayri paylasimli bellek (s_sum + 32), cagri 2*32 float.
Etki: satir > 32 olan softmax'ta (VoxCPM2 on doldurma dikkati) ayni tohum/ayar ile her kosuda farkli ses.
Sonrasi: ayni okuma bayt bayt ayni (3 satir x 2 kosu, GTX 1050 Ti). Hesap degismez, yalniz senkronizasyon.

Port of upstream audio.cpp PR #837 (ggml #26385) to v0.7.2: shared-memory race between consecutive
block_reduce calls in soft_max_f32 / single-row softmax / group_norm_f32 made identical inputs give
different bytes. Apply after 0001 and 0002.

diff --git a/external/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/norm.cu b/external/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/norm.cu
index ef98f67..7fdd501 100644
--- a/external/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/norm.cu
+++ b/external/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/norm.cu
@@ -62,7 +62,8 @@ static __global__ void group_norm_f32(const float * x, float * dst, const int gr
         tmp += xi * xi;
     }
 
-    tmp = block_reduce<block_reduce_method::SUM, block_size>(tmp, s_sum);
+    // ahenk yama c4a (upstream #837): ikinci azaltma ayri paylasimli bellek kullanir / second reduction uses its own buffer
+    tmp = block_reduce<block_reduce_method::SUM, block_size>(tmp, s_sum + 32);
 
     const float variance = tmp / group_size;
     const float scale = rsqrtf(variance + eps);
@@ -290,7 +291,7 @@ static void group_norm_f32_cuda(
         group_norm_f32<WARP_SIZE><<<num_groups, block_dims, 0, stream>>>(x, dst, group_size, ne_elements, eps);
     } else {
         const dim3 block_dims(1024, 1, 1);
-        group_norm_f32<1024><<<num_groups, block_dims, block_dims.x > WARP_SIZE ? 32 * sizeof(float): 0, stream>>>(x, dst, group_size, ne_elements, eps);
+        group_norm_f32<1024><<<num_groups, block_dims, block_dims.x > WARP_SIZE ? 2 * 32 * sizeof(float): 0, stream>>>(x, dst, group_size, ne_elements, eps);
     }
 }
 
